     "content": "The user wants me to act as the Skeptic and evaluate two crime pairs. I need to return a JSON object with verdicts for each pair: approve, send_back, or drop, with critique and optional requery.\n\nLet me analyze each pair carefully.\n\nPair 1: CHN-AD-2026-001182 | CHN-TI-2026-001148\n- Crime A: Oct 14, 19:40, LB Road near Adyar bus depot, plate TN09??4471, red Bajaj Pulsar 150\n- Crime B: Oct 7, 20:34, near Tidel Park, Thiruvanmiyur, plate null, red Bajaj Pulsar 150\n- Distance: 1.5 km, Days apart: 7\n- MO similarity: 0.9 (very high)\n- Space-time: 0.44 (moderate)\n- Vehicle: 0.85 (strong - same make/model/color, partial plate match, ANPR hits ANPR-R0585086 and ANPR-R0590687)\n- Suspect description: 1.0 (identical)\n- Target profile: 1.0 (identical)\n- Score: 0.819, band: high\n\nThis looks very strong. Near-identical MO, same suspect description, same target, same vehicle type/color, ANPR hits linking the vehicle across locations. The partial plate TN09??4471 matches the pattern. The 7 days and 1.5 km is tight. I'd approve.\n\nPair 2: CHN-AD-2026-001182 | CHN-VL-2026-000877\n- Crime A: Oct 14, 19:40, LB Road near Adyar bus depot, plate TN09??4471\n- Crime B: Oct 16, 19:55, Velachery Main Road near Vijaya Nagar bus stop, plate TN09B?4471\n- Distance: 3.5 km, Days apart: 2\n- MO similarity: 0.88 (high, violence differs slightly: push vs push_and_fall)\n- Space-time: 0.33 (moderate)\n- Vehicle: 0.85 (strong - same make/model/color, plates TN09??4471 and TN09B?4471 are very similar, ANPR hits ANPR-R0590687 and ANPR-R0592410)\n- Suspect description: 1.0 (identical)\n- Target profile: 1.0 (identical)\n- Score: 0.7887, band: high\n\nAlso very strong. Two days apart, 3.5 km, nearly identical plates (TN09??4471 vs TN09B?4471 - the B could be the missing character), ANPR hits. The violence difference is minor (push vs push_and_fall). This also looks like a strong link.\n\nBoth pairs have high scores, strong vehicle linkage with ANPR evidence, identical suspect descriptions, identical target profiles, and high MO similarity. The spatiotemporal proximity is good (7 days/1.5km and 2 days/3.5km). These are not just same area coincidences - they have multiple strong linking factors.\n\nI should approve both. No need for requery. The evidence is solid.\n\nLet me construct the JSON.</think>{\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"CHN-AD-2026-001182|CHN-TI-2026-001148\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"approve\",\n      \"critique\": \"Near-identical MO (0.9), suspect description (1.0), and target profile (1.0). Vehicle linkage is strong: same red Bajaj Pulsar 150, partial plate TN09??4471 matches pattern, and two ANPR hits (ANPR-R0585086, ANPR-R0590687) place the vehicle across both locations. Spatiotemporal proximity is tight (1.5 km, 7 days). Multiple independent evidence streams converge.\",\n      \"requery\": null\n    },\n    \"CHN-AD-2026-001182|CHN-VL-2026-000877\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"approve\",\n      \"critique\": \"MO similarity 0.88 (only violence differs: push vs push_and_fall), suspect description 1.0, target profile 1.0. Vehicle linkage is strong: plates TN09??4471 and TN09B?4471 are highly consistent (B likely fills a wildcard), same make/model/color, and two ANPR hits (ANPR-R0590687, ANPR-R0592410). Spatiotemporal proximity is very tight (3.5 km, 2 days). The combination of vehicle plate pattern, ANPR corroboration, and behavioral consistency makes this a credible series link.\",\n      \"requery\": null\n    }\n  }\n}"
